analysis.method:
Using a modified CRPropa3 Monte Carlo code, the authors model 3D electromagnetic cascades for sources at $z \le 2$ embedded in filaments ($B_{\mathrm{fil}} = 30\,\mathrm{nG}$, $l_c = 100\,\mathrm{kpc}$) and voids ($B_{\mathrm{void}} = 10^{-16}	ext{--}10^{-19}\,\mathrm{G}$, $l_c = 1\,\mathrm{Mpc}$), combining $p\gamma$ production relations $ rac{1}{3}\sum_{\alpha}\varepsilon_{
u}\mathcal{E}_{\varepsilon_{
u_{\alpha}}}\approx rac{K_{\pi}}{4}[\varepsilon_{\gamma}\mathcal{E}_{\varepsilon_{\gamma}}]_{\varepsilon_{\gamma}=2\varepsilon_{
u}}$ ($K_\pi \approx 1$) with cooling length $D_{\mathrm{IC}}= rac{3m_e^2 c^4}{4\sigma_T u_{\mathrm{CMB}}\varepsilon_e} \propto (1+z)^{-4}$.

